      cards: [
        ['Thread', 'A unit of execution inside a process: own PC, registers, stack; shares code, data, heap, files.'],
        ['Four benefits', 'Responsiveness · Resource sharing · Economy · Scalability.'],
        ['Concurrency', 'More than one task making progress — possible on one core by switching.'],
        ['Parallelism', 'More than one task executing simultaneously — needs multiple cores.'],
        ['Data parallelism', 'Same operation on different subsets of data on each core (e.g. partial sums).'],
        ['Task parallelism', 'Different operations on different threads/cores (render, decode, JS).'],
        ['Amdahl\'s Law', 'speedup ≤ 1 / (S + (1−S)/N). As N → ∞, speedup → 1/S.'],
        ['User vs kernel threads', 'User: managed by a library, kernel unaware, one blocks → all block. Kernel: managed by the OS, scheduled independently.'],
        ['Many-to-one', 'Many user threads → 1 kernel thread. No parallelism; one block blocks all. (Green threads — rare)'],
        ['One-to-one', 'Each user thread → its own kernel thread. True parallelism. Linux, Windows.'],
        ['Many-to-many', 'Many user threads → many (≤) kernel threads. Flexible, rare (Windows ThreadFiber).'],
        ['pthread_create', 'pthread_create(&tid, attr, runner, arg) — runner is void *runner(void *arg).'],
        ['pthread_join', 'Waits for a thread to finish (like wait() for processes).'],
        ['Thread pool', 'Pre-created threads take tasks from a queue — faster, bounded, flexible.'],
        ['Fork-join', 'Fork subtasks into threads, join to collect results (merge sort, parallel sum).'],
        ['OpenMP', '#pragma omp parallel for — compiler creates the threads. gcc -fopenmp.'],
        ['Deferred cancellation', 'Thread checks pthread_testcancel() at safe points. Default in Pthreads. Async = dangerous.'],
        ['Thread-local storage', 'Per-thread copy of a variable across function calls: __thread / _Thread_local.'],
        ['clone()', 'Linux syscall behind threads; flags (CLONE_VM, CLONE_FILES, CLONE_SIGHAND, CLONE_THREAD) choose what is shared.'],
        ['Scheduler activations', 'Kernel upcalls to the thread library to keep the right number of LWPs (many-to-many). Mostly historical.'],
      ],
